Subject: [PATCH 14/14] bridge: mute/volume for the engine SDL audio path

The GetAudio ring carries PinMAME ROM sound only; table script sounds
(sound effects) play through the engine's own SDL audio devices and
ignore the host WebAudio gain, so UI mute left effects audible. Add
VpxWasm_SetAudioLevel: an overall output level driving both buses via
the desktop UpdateVolume path, so the host mute/volume control fans
out to script sounds too. The table-seeded bus volumes hold until the
host first calls this; unmute restores the host level to both buses
(the table music/sound split is not preserved across the first call).
Volume is clamped at the boundary (AudioStreamPlayer takes sqrtf of
the bus volume with no saturation). ROM audio keeps its host-side
gain. Rebuild with wasm/build-headless.sh.

Target: vpinball/vpinball@64a480a96d1b972711fbb8eea014654c779b1e23

diff --git a/src/web/vpx_wasm_bridge.cpp b/src/web/vpx_wasm_bridge.cpp
--- a/src/web/vpx_wasm_bridge.cpp
+++ b/src/web/vpx_wasm_bridge.cpp
@@ -661,7 +661,25 @@ EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE void VpxWasm_Nudge(float angleDeg, float force)
 {
    if (!g_player)
       return;
    g_player->m_pininput.m_nudgeHandler->ApplyKeyboardImpulse(angleDeg, force);
 }
 
+// Overall output level for the engine's own SDL audio path (table script
+// sounds); PinMAME ROM audio rides the GetAudio ring and is gained on the
+// host. Mute zeroes both buses via the desktop UpdateVolume path, so live
+// voices go quiet too. Table-seeded volumes hold until the host calls this;
+// unmute then restores the host level to both buses (not the table split).
+// Volume is clamped at the boundary: AudioStreamPlayer takes sqrtf of the
+// bus volume with no saturation, so a negative input would yield NaN gain.
+EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE void VpxWasm_SetAudioLevel(float volume, int muted)
+{
+   if (!g_player)
+      return;
+   const float clamped = (volume < 0.f) ? 0.f : ((volume > 1.f) ? 1.f : volume);
+   const float level = (muted != 0) ? 0.f : clamped;
+   g_player->m_backglassVolume = level;
+   g_player->m_playfieldVolume = level;
+   g_player->UpdateVolume();
+}
+
